    {
      "id": "claim_dd1f99b26ed04b249820703650e9eaba",
      "statement": "Deleting a thread (server/threads.py delete_thread) cascades a best-effort cleanup: it deletes the thread registry record, the graph checkpoints via saver.adelete_thread, all run registry records for that thread, all cron registry records scoped to that thread, and any in-memory RunEngine runtime/queue entries for those runs; each cascade step is wrapped so a failure is logged rather than silently swallowed or fatal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/threads.py#L429-L498",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:32124637638f6f92d587d997390a0fada83609b9ef496acf7e8d697acbe42703:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1d2cc3de7cfb4f95a8fc85a862d17eb1",
      "statement": "server/storage.py create_storage() selects the storage backend from SERVER_STORAGE: the memory backend (default) uses InMemorySaver/InMemoryStore plus in-process dict-backed MemoryRegistries for threads/runs/crons, so nothing survives a process restart; the postgres backend uses AsyncPostgresSaver/AsyncPostgresStore over one shared pooled AsyncConnectionPool plus PostgresRegistries-backed durable hc_threads/hc_runs/hc_crons tables.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/registries.py#L121-L153",
