    {
      "id": "claim_5c20155fcd1d472db4710ccb02fc644e",
      "statement": "create_storage falls back to a lexical-only store (index=None) instead of failing startup when embeddings are unavailable (missing/invalid API key, import/runtime errors) or, on the Postgres path, when the pgvector `vector` extension is unavailable, logging a warning in both cases; non-vector Postgres setup errors are not swallowed and propagate so a deploy fails visibly, and the connection pool is closed before re-raising to avoid leaking it.",
