    {
      "id": "claim_74006a786c50416c945b45ba271922e3",
      "statement": "The Postgres storage test lane is run via `make server-test-pg`, which brings up a disposable compose Postgres container and runs tests/server/test_registries.py, test_threads_postgres.py, test_runs_durable.py, test_crons_postgres.py, and test_storage_postgres.py against it (plus scripts/pg_lane_concurrent.py for the advisory-lock race), then tears the container and volume down; tests/server/test_postgres_durability_gaps.py is gated the same way behind a POSTGRES_TEST_DSN env var via its postgres_url fixture and skips cleanly when unset, but is not included in the make target's file list and must be run explicitly. The memory-backed path is exercised by the rest of tests/server/ under plain `make server-test`.",
